{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/933780-combat-tweaking-a-nuwisha","id":933780,"title":"Combat tweaking a .... Nuwisha ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-19T01:34:51-07:00","id":933780,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Combat tweaking a .... Nuwisha ?","content":"As it has been said, spending Rage for additional actions is hugely imbalanced in regards to all the beings, who can't do it...<br /> <br /> And I know that there is a level 3 gift, that allows to gain 5 Rage, to spend on additional actions once per scene.<br /> <br /> But I was wondering, what other ideas you have for gifts or fetishes, talens etc. that could increase a nuwishas combat skills (preferably at rank 1)....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 07-19-2016, 04:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T06:39:08-07:00","id":933841,"title":"","content":"Nuwisha are not combat monsters, though they can gain Gifts later on that make them surprisingly good fighters. They are meant to be jokers and saboteurs, not warriors. That being said, Coyote's Fang (a level three fetish) is an obvious choice, as it does aggravated damage across the spiritual divide, allowing a Nuwisha could use it to attack a spirit from the material world or a material opponent from the spiritual world. That one fetish upgrades Nuwisha from amusing comics to undetectable assassins.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T07:35:13-07:00","id":933868,"title":"","content":"Nice fetish, but it doesn't grant seeing through the Gauntlet. So, one has to use the Peeking rules. Not that easy. Also revised has a similar Theurge gift. Still, not a bad choice...<br /> It'll make my list.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T07:57:33-07:00","id":933887,"title":"","content":"Toss in Loki as a totem, gives you an extra health level and extra physical dot","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T11:00:27-07:00","id":933980,"title":"","content":"Oghma also grants four extra Physical Attribute does when teaching someone humility. You could use Coyote's Fang to do that with a little creativity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T12:56:01-07:00","id":934038,"title":"","content":"What of using bottomless clip talons.. John Woo specials they are often called.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T02:32:56-07:00","id":934363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/933780-combat-tweaking-a-nuwisha?p=933868#post933868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice fetish, but it doesn't grant seeing through the Gauntlet. So, one has to use the Peeking rules. Not that easy. Also revised has a similar Theurge gift. Still, not a bad choice...<br /> It'll make my list.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could combo it with that Gift that allowed you spiritsight onto the other side at will?<br /> <br /> Also, I'd look into alternative methods of Combat then brute force. Ranged weaponry bound with spirits can really mess people's day. From the trivial - Fang Dagger bullets/arrows/rocks to the insane like getting pain spirits, electricity spirits, gun spirits or even atomic spirits into your weapons to clear the house out or provide utility.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T03:17:14-07:00","id":934376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/933780-combat-tweaking-a-nuwisha?p=934363#post934363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could combo it with that Gift that allowed you spiritsight onto the other side at will?</div> </div> </div> </div>That be rank 3, iirc. A bit high, especially for a gift that one can't learn from one's own list.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/933780-combat-tweaking-a-nuwisha?p=934363#post934363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I'd look into alternative methods of Combat then brute force. Ranged weaponry bound with spirits can really mess people's day. From the trivial - Fang Dagger bullets/arrows/rocks to the insane like getting pain spirits, electricity spirits, gun spirits or even atomic spirits into your weapons to clear the house out or provide utility.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was looking for printed material, for I didn't want to start in a new troupe with bargaining to much for non-printed stuff.<br /> <br /> Fang Dagger however is a choice that will make my list. Thanks. I think &quot;Hunter Talons&quot; are equally helpful...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T04:03:46-07:00","id":934388,"title":"","content":"Something defensive, maybe. Increasing soak or means not to get hit with multiple attacks in a round would be nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T12:06:46-07:00","id":934638,"title":"","content":"I think you would be depending more on stealth as a Nuwisha. Military grade sniper rifles, especially equipped with sabot silver rounds to protect the internal rifling, would be able to kill almost anything in the WoD. You would be able to slip into the Umbra after the kill, which would make you nearly impossible to catch, though you will have to scout out the Umbra before you make the kill to make sure you do not end up somewhere bad...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T01:00:08-07:00","id":934952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/933780-combat-tweaking-a-nuwisha?p=934388#post934388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something defensive, maybe. Increasing soak or means not to get hit with multiple attacks in a round would be nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a collar(?) that makes it higher difficulty to be hit in Hammer and Klaive? Something like that could help you out, especially as you could scale its effect with Fetish level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T05:04:29-07:00","id":934999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/933780-combat-tweaking-a-nuwisha?p=934952#post934952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a collar(?) that makes it higher difficulty to be hit in Hammer and Klaive? Something like that could help you out, especially as you could scale its effect with Fetish level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Full text searched &quot;collar&quot; and &quot;to hit&quot; but didn't find it. But, yes something like that would be nice.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T23:26:26-07:00","id":935465,"title":"","content":"So, build the character for a new troupe yesterday. Since the troupe was limited to W20 line books, I choose 'Phobe's Veil' which is usually a quite solid defensive tool. I mean, unless someone touches you, you are basically undetectable, and therefore can't get attacked, no matter how often a garou could act in a turn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}